# The operator: *"i played 'Cry of Contrition' which has haunt. i expect to
# see the 'haunt' keyword on my creature."* Seat 0 (human)
# holds Cry of Contrition (`{B}`) and one untapped Swamp — enough to cast it —
# plus her own Memnite on the battlefield, the only creature on the table.
# An uncontested turn-1 Main Phase 1.
#
# Cry of Contrition's own ability (`K:Haunt:TrigDiscard`, `res/cardsfolder/c/
# cry_of_contrition.txt`) targets a PLAYER ("Target player discards a card.");
# alice targets herself, so nothing about this scenario needs bob to act at
# all. Once it resolves and goes to the graveyard, Haunt's own trigger
# (`CardFactoryUtil.java:1254-1262`, `DB$ Haunt | ValidTgts$ Creature |
# TgtPrompt$ Choose target creature to haunt`) fires and asks for a target
# creature — Memnite is the only legal one, so the haunt pairing this test
# needs is reached by ordinary play, never scripted directly: `GameState`
# (`apps/server/src/play/scenarios/README.md`) has no key for a haunt
# relation, because Forge's own state has none either until the ability
# actually resolves.
turn=1
activeplayer=human
activephase=MAIN1
humanlife=20
ailife=20
humanhand=Cry of Contrition;Mountain
humanbattlefield=Swamp;Memnite
humanlibrary=Swamp;Swamp;Swamp;Swamp
humangraveyard=
aihand=
aibattlefield=
ailibrary=Swamp;Swamp;Swamp;Swamp
aigraveyard=
